ile+os.replace of a full snapshot with NO advisory/file lock and NO read-merge step. No existing lock-protected read-merge-write path for these JSON sidecars is demonstrated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa3263854c1ca61ee","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach: 'Use the existing locked store boundary for read-merge-write'","norm_id":"nb12b85bbea34b42e","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author designs the fix around reusing commit_tickets_branch's lock, discovers it does not cover the in-memory-record merge, and the read-merge-write must be built fresh (advisory lock around load+merge+save)."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"high","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the locked read-merge-write reconciles DELETIONS (e.g. diff the in-memory set against the pre-write baseline and apply removals, or tombstone) so records intentionally dropped by should_skip are not resurrected by the merge, and add a test covering delete-during-concurrent-write.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1778,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["impossible_links.should_skip deletes stale records and marks dirty: 'del self._records[record_key(...)]' then 'self._dirty = True' (impossible_links.py:321-322)","Docstring rationale for the delete: 'a link that became possible leaves a dead entry in the file forever, and the store grows without bound' (impossible_links.py:318-320)","Plan Approach says 'Preserve distinct keys under concurrent writers' and 'deterministic same-key resolution' but never addresses keys REMOVED from the in-memory set relative to disk"],"finding":"The read-merge-write mechanism does not account for record DELETIONS, so a merge that unions on-disk records with in-memory records will resurrect entries the pass intentionally removed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f02a1b6a2dad1ecf4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Acceptance Criteria (distinct-key retention)","norm_id":"n33461846b557e443","priority":0.7778,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A pass calls should_skip, drops a now-possible link, then saves; the merge re-reads the still-present on-disk key and re-adds it -> the impossible-link store grows unbounded again","Two concurrent passes where one deletes a key the other never touched: union merge keeps the deleted key alive"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribu